  "F5 pivot": {
   "range": "toes roll up; digit III pivots on its claw",
   "value": "toe pad edge, a transition arc, then the middle claw tip (gait.roll_offset)",
   "rule": "A rigid foot pitched heel-up about its toe pad's front edge touches the floor with the middle claw at 0.08 rad (60 cm) / 0.07 rad (75 cm) and then rolls on the claw tip, as digit III does in birds; the reference rolls it so, over a short transition arc (no part below the floor).  The plant has no contact on the claws (contype 0), so in simulation the claw passes through the floor and a controller cannot load it; on the hardware the claw tip would carry the trailing foot's load through the roll.  For the owner: a load-bearing claw tip (and claw contact in the plant), a shorter claw (the roll then stays on the pad edge), or a toe-off capped near 0.07-0.08 rad."
