 "method": "The stance pad's single-support yaw moment against the tail's phase on one walk.  The walk runs with no tail and with ``amp`` at each of ``phases``; per frame M_z = A + B cos(p) + C sin(p) is fitted (the tail's effect is linear at these amplitudes; the fit's residual and the no-tail run against A are reported), its peak |M_z| is minimised over ``grid`` phases, and the walk is run again at the minimiser to confirm it.  Today's phase is pi/2 (``gait.GaitSpec.tail_phase``); research Bottom line 4 reads it as adding to the legs' yaw momentum.",
 "convention": "tail = tail_amp sin(2 pi phase + tail_phase), phase 0 at the left foot's lift-off; a positive tail_yaw swings the tip to the robot's right (axis about +z); today's tail_phase is pi/2"
}